# Run: dotnet run --project samples/Orders.Api
@host = http://localhost:5390

### First page: 10 orders, newest first (OrderDto's default sort)
GET {{host}}/orders?per_page=10

### Page 2, by customer name, then newest first within each customer
GET {{host}}/orders?page=2&per_page=10&sort=customer_name,created_at:desc

### Keys in any casing name the same properties: CustomerName, createdAt, customer-name
GET {{host}}/orders?per_page=5&sort=CustomerName:desc,createdAt

### 400: total isn't sortable; the error names what is, in snake_case
GET {{host}}/orders?sort=total

### Every order in one query (PagingParams.All), oldest id first
GET {{host}}/orders/export?sort=id

### In memory, no database: customers by country, then name (names sort case-insensitively)
GET {{host}}/customers?per_page=3&sort=country,name

### Out-of-range paging falls back to the defaults (page 1, 100 per page)
GET {{host}}/customers?page=0&per_page=-5
